WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:29.940
Honsu represents water.

00:29.940 --> 00:34.800
Honsu is the source of life that nurtures the will and spirit to embrace all.

00:34.800 --> 00:40.220
The progress line of Honsu Pumse that represents the unity harmonized through the movement

00:40.220 --> 00:47.140
of attack and defense expressed in a diagonal formation is the character Su, which means

00:47.140 --> 00:49.100
water.

00:49.100 --> 00:52.460
We will now take a look at the key moves of Honsu Pumse.

01:19.100 --> 01:38.340
Honsu is the source of life that nurtures the will and spirit to embrace all.

01:38.340 --> 02:06.420
Honsu Pumse consists of six key moves, namely Son-nal-deung-hae-cheon-mak-i, Mae-jumok-yang-yeop-guri-an-chigi,

02:06.420 --> 02:25.420
Kkoduro-kalchebi, Anpal-mok-arae-pyojak-mak-i, Son-nal-geum-gang-mak-i, and Kkyeot-dari-seo-gi.

02:25.420 --> 02:30.100
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Honsu Pumse.

02:30.100 --> 02:36.100
Son-nal-deung-hae-cheon-mak-i is a technique to cross the two hands in front of the chest

02:36.100 --> 02:40.100
and block by scattering them sideways.

02:40.100 --> 02:48.340
When performing Momtong-hae-cheon-mak-i, the tip of the hand must not rise above the shoulder.

02:48.340 --> 02:53.300
Attach your armpits to your body to make them firm and the tip of your hand and elbow must

02:53.300 --> 02:57.500
be placed in the same line.

02:57.500 --> 03:04.740
Cross the arm of the forward foot from the outside.

03:04.740 --> 03:11.860
Mae-jumok-yang-yeop-guri-an-chigi is a technique to strike both sides of the waist outside in

03:11.860 --> 03:17.340
with both fists elevated to about one fist length above the shoulder.

03:17.340 --> 03:21.700
Attach the armpit firmly to the body to concentrate force.

03:21.700 --> 03:26.700
The fist should be placed slightly over the elbow.

03:26.700 --> 03:29.940
The elbows should be close to the torso.

03:29.940 --> 03:34.300
Be careful not to let the fists rise excessively.

03:34.300 --> 03:40.500
Godoro-kaljebi is a technique used to block an opponent's attack by pressing with the palm of your hand

03:40.500 --> 03:44.220
and attack an opponent's neck with an arc fist.

03:44.220 --> 03:49.220
Strike an opponent with the arched part of the arc fist.

03:49.220 --> 03:56.220
Concentrate and transfer force by making the surface area of the target small.

03:56.220 --> 04:02.220
The elbow of the arm that performed kaljebi should lightly touch the back of the assisting hand

04:02.340 --> 04:05.940
and straighten the wrist so it doesn't bend.

04:05.940 --> 04:14.940
Anpal-mok-are-pyo-jok-mak-gi is used to create a target at shoulder elevation with the arc fist of the hand performing aremak-gi,

04:14.940 --> 04:19.740
where the inner wrist touches between the thumb and index finger to block.

04:19.740 --> 04:28.180
It is important to fix the hand acting as a target in front of the lower abdomen and only move the arm blocking the lower body.

04:28.180 --> 04:33.780
When performing seon-na-geun-gang-mak-gi, the hand blade and center line should be aligned.

04:33.780 --> 04:39.180
Be careful not to let the elbow of the arm blocking the face rise first.

04:39.180 --> 04:43.940
Gyeot-dari-seo-gi is a standing posture where one leg acts as support.

04:43.940 --> 04:49.340
The opposite big toe touches the ground in the middle of the back of the supporting foot blade,

04:49.340 --> 04:53.040
and the rear sole is slightly raised.

04:53.040 --> 04:59.440
Both feet slightly touch each other and stand with the knees facing forward.

04:59.440 --> 05:03.240
The knees should not be apart.

05:03.240 --> 05:08.840
Be careful not to let the upper body swerve forward.

05:08.840 --> 05:14.560
These are the 6 key moves of hansu-pum-se.

05:14.560 --> 05:22.760
We will now look at the moves in succession, connecting each move.

05:22.760 --> 05:29.760
The key moves of hansu first part consist of

05:29.760 --> 05:32.120
seon-nal-deung-hae-cheo-mak-gi

05:32.120 --> 05:34.120
mae-joo-mok-an-cheo-gi

05:34.120 --> 05:37.120
mul-lo-di-jeo-wae-san-teul-mak-gi

05:37.120 --> 05:38.760
eo-reun-ji-reu-gi

05:38.760 --> 05:41.760
mul-lo-di-jeo-wae-san-teul-mak-gi

05:41.760 --> 05:43.160
wae-n-ji-reu-gi

05:43.160 --> 05:45.960
mul-lo-di-jeo-wae-san-teul-mak-gi

05:45.960 --> 05:47.680
eo-reun-ji-reu-gi

05:47.680 --> 05:52.480
and seon-nal-deung-hae-cheo-mak-gi

05:52.480 --> 05:55.400
Because you set the left foot when you start,

05:55.400 --> 05:58.200
you must perform seon-nal-deung-hae-cheo-mak-gi

05:58.200 --> 06:00.680
by switching hands from jeop-seon,

06:00.680 --> 06:05.080
so the left arm crosses outside.

06:05.080 --> 06:09.200
When performing mae-joo-mok-an-cheo-gi,

06:09.200 --> 06:16.800
the two hammer fists strike both sides of the waist outside in

06:16.800 --> 06:21.200
while the armpits touch the body.

06:21.200 --> 06:24.400
When connecting to wae-san-teul-mak-gi,

06:24.400 --> 06:29.400
the blocking arm should move past the face to protect it.

06:29.400 --> 06:32.400
After completing wae-san-teul-mak-gi,

06:32.400 --> 06:36.920
place both feet on the same line slightly tilted.

06:36.920 --> 06:41.720
Move and set the opposite foot facing the same direction as your gaze,

06:41.720 --> 06:45.920
then connect to mon-do-ra-i-di-di-myo-ji-ri-gi.

06:47.200 --> 06:49.920
Cautions for hansu first part.

06:49.920 --> 06:54.520
Taking a closer look.

06:54.520 --> 06:58.040
When connecting from wae-san-teul-mak-gi to jir-gi,

06:58.040 --> 07:01.840
be careful not to change elevation.

07:01.840 --> 07:07.920
It is important to perform all these motions naturally without disconnect.

07:07.920 --> 07:11.840
We will now practice the moves of hansu first part in succession

07:11.840 --> 07:14.840
while watching the video.

07:19.920 --> 07:33.240
The key moves of hansu second part consist of

07:33.240 --> 07:35.720
kodoro-agum-son-ap-chigi,

07:35.720 --> 07:37.880
du-jumok-cheot-chyeo-jir-gi,

07:37.880 --> 07:40.640
wen-agum-son-pyo-jeo-are-mak-gi,

07:40.640 --> 07:42.720
son-nal-keum-gang-mak-gi,

07:42.720 --> 07:45.320
hak-dar-i-seo-gi chageun-dol-jeo-gi,

07:45.320 --> 07:48.840
jop-chagi and jae-bi-pum-an-chigi,

07:48.840 --> 07:53.360
and orun-ap-chagi and du-jumok-ap-chigi.

07:53.360 --> 07:56.240
When performing kodoro-agum-son-ap-chigi,

07:56.240 --> 07:59.000
press and block with the right palm of your hand

07:59.000 --> 08:03.400
and perform ap-chigi with the left arc fist at the same time.

08:03.400 --> 08:10.800
The left elbow should touch the top of the back of the right hand.

08:10.800 --> 08:12.440
In kyeot-dar-i-seo-gi,

08:12.440 --> 08:17.900
the hind leg disrupts the motion from the leg that ran and set first,

08:17.900 --> 08:19.320
maintains a center,

08:19.320 --> 08:23.800
then transfer force to the fist.

08:23.800 --> 08:26.400
When performing wen-pyo-jeok-are-mak-gi,

08:26.400 --> 08:32.060
strike as if inserting the right inner wrist into the left arc fist.

08:32.060 --> 08:37.460
Do not move the left hand and block with the right inner wrist.

08:37.460 --> 08:40.400
When setting back with son-nal-keum-gang-mak-gi,

08:40.400 --> 08:45.220
be careful not to change elevation.

08:45.240 --> 08:51.040
Change direction for hak-dar-i-seo-gi jageun-do-jeok-ui 90 degrees.

08:51.040 --> 08:55.040
The move and the spin must complete at the same time.

08:55.040 --> 08:56.680
When performing ap-chagi,

08:56.680 --> 08:59.880
both hands should be placed naturally inside the body

08:59.880 --> 09:03.820
to avoid any inconvenience when kicking.

09:03.820 --> 09:07.180
Perform jjichigi with the forward kicking foot

09:07.180 --> 09:10.980
and stop momentum with the left foot.

09:10.980 --> 09:12.740
After achieving balance,

09:12.740 --> 09:14.360
transfer force to the fist

09:14.360 --> 09:18.460
and connect to deung-jung-mok ap-chigi along with a shout.

09:21.900 --> 09:27.300
Cautions for hansu second part, taking a closer look.

09:27.300 --> 09:30.060
When performing du-jung-mok-jeot-jeo-chir-gi,

09:30.060 --> 09:36.260
be careful not to let the armpits move away from the body.

09:36.260 --> 09:39.200
When performing wen-pyo-jeok-are-mak-gi,

09:39.200 --> 09:41.760
pay attention to the direction of your gaze,

09:41.760 --> 09:47.020
just like the previous move.

09:47.020 --> 09:48.780
Perform o-ren ap-chagi

09:48.780 --> 09:52.360
through the coordination of the upper and lower body.

09:52.360 --> 09:55.620
Do not use only the left leg when kicking

09:55.620 --> 09:59.020
and do not kick above the head.

09:59.020 --> 10:02.160
We will now practice the moves of hansu second part

10:02.160 --> 10:04.660
in succession while watching the video.

10:11.760 --> 10:21.220
The key moves of hansu third part consist of

10:21.220 --> 10:22.960
wen-seon-ah-yeop-chigi

10:22.960 --> 10:25.260
o-ren-pal-nal-deung-pyo-jeok-chagi

10:25.260 --> 10:27.760
o-ren-pal-kkum-chi-pyo-jeok-chigi

10:27.760 --> 10:30.320
kkeo-deu-ro o-ren-a-geum-seon-ap-chigi

10:30.320 --> 10:32.820
du-ju-mok-cheot-jeo-jir-gi

10:32.820 --> 10:35.460
o-ren-a-geum-seon-pyo-jeok-are-mak-gi

10:35.460 --> 10:39.580
and son-na-geum-gang-mak-gi.

10:39.600 --> 10:42.040
When performing wen-seon-ah-yeop-chigi,

10:42.040 --> 10:44.080
the lower body should stand firm

10:44.080 --> 10:47.140
and make use of the torque of the spin.

10:47.140 --> 10:48.980
It is important that your eyes point

10:48.980 --> 10:51.900
in the direction of progression.

10:51.900 --> 10:54.100
o-ren-pal-nal-deung-pyo-jeok-chigi

10:54.100 --> 10:57.180
is a technique that uses the back of the foot blade

10:57.180 --> 11:00.780
and is performed in succession with pyo-jeok-chigi.

11:00.780 --> 11:02.980
After performing pyo-jeok-chigi,

11:02.980 --> 11:05.140
turn to the direction of progression

11:05.140 --> 11:08.500
and stand with the feet gathered together.

11:10.400 --> 11:15.000
Then, continue with kkeo-deu-ro o-kal-je-pi.

11:15.000 --> 11:16.680
In kkeot-dari-seo-gi,

11:16.680 --> 11:19.340
the hind leg stops the moment of the leg

11:19.340 --> 11:23.340
that ran and set first,

11:23.340 --> 11:24.940
maintains a center,

11:24.940 --> 11:28.940
then transfers force to the fist.

11:28.940 --> 11:31.400
When performing pyo-jeok-are-mak-gi,

11:31.400 --> 11:33.500
fix the right arc fist,

11:33.500 --> 11:35.080
then strike and block

11:35.080 --> 11:39.180
like you're inserting the left inner wrist.

11:39.200 --> 11:42.500
When setting your foot back with sona kkeum-gang-mak-gi,

11:42.500 --> 11:46.400
be careful not to change elevation.

11:46.400 --> 11:48.900
Cautions for hansu third part,

11:48.900 --> 11:50.980
taking a closer look.

11:50.980 --> 11:53.040
When performing pyo-jeok-chigi,

11:53.040 --> 11:55.680
be mindful to use the back of the foot blade

11:55.680 --> 11:58.680
rather than the sole.

12:00.340 --> 12:03.300
Also, remember that the target must not move

12:03.300 --> 12:07.300
during pyo-jeok-are-mak-gi.

12:09.700 --> 12:12.700
We will now practice the moves of hansu third part

12:12.700 --> 12:16.700
in succession while watching the video.

12:27.500 --> 12:29.580
The key moves of hansu fourth part

12:29.580 --> 12:31.180
consist of

12:31.180 --> 12:34.440
hak-dari-seo-gi chageun-dol-jeok-gi,

12:34.440 --> 12:35.680
or-eun-yeop-chagi,

12:35.680 --> 12:37.680
jebi-pum-an-chigi,

12:37.680 --> 12:38.800
wen-ap-chagi,

12:38.820 --> 12:40.820
wen-deung-jumeok-ap-chigi,

12:40.820 --> 12:42.820
or-eun-seon-na-yeop-chigi,

12:42.820 --> 12:44.320
wen-pyo-jeok-chagi,

12:44.320 --> 12:48.320
and wen-pal-kum-chi-pyo-jeok-chigi.

12:49.320 --> 12:51.320
Change direction 90 degrees

12:51.320 --> 12:55.820
when performing hak-dari-seo-gi chageun-dol-jeok-gi.

12:55.820 --> 12:57.820
Change direction at the same time

12:57.820 --> 13:02.820
while assuming the hak-dari-seo-gi posture.

13:02.820 --> 13:05.320
When connecting to ap-chagi,

13:05.320 --> 13:07.320
both hands should be placed naturally

13:07.340 --> 13:11.840
inside the body to easily assist the kick.

13:11.840 --> 13:13.840
Next, perform chi-chigi

13:13.840 --> 13:15.840
with the front foot that kicked.

13:15.840 --> 13:17.840
Stop motion with the left foot

13:17.840 --> 13:19.840
and achieve balance.

13:19.840 --> 13:21.840
Then, transfer force to the back

13:21.840 --> 13:24.840
of the left fist along with a shout.

13:27.840 --> 13:30.840
When performing or-eun-seon-na-yeop-chigi,

13:30.840 --> 13:32.840
the lower body should stand firm

13:32.840 --> 13:35.840
and make use of the torque of the spin.

13:35.860 --> 13:37.860
It is important that your eyes

13:37.860 --> 13:40.360
point in the direction of progression.

13:40.360 --> 13:43.360
When performing wen-pyo-jeok-chagi,

13:43.360 --> 13:45.360
use the back of the foot blade

13:45.360 --> 13:48.360
then connect naturally to pyo-jeok-chigi.

13:53.360 --> 13:56.360
Cautions for hansu fourth part,

13:56.360 --> 13:58.360
taking a closer look.

13:58.360 --> 14:00.360
Remember that you must use

14:00.360 --> 14:01.860
the back of the foot blade

14:01.860 --> 14:02.860
rather than the sole

14:02.880 --> 14:04.880
when performing pyo-jeok-chagi.

14:07.380 --> 14:09.380
Remember that the arm on the same side

14:09.380 --> 14:12.380
as the set foot must be on the outside.

14:26.380 --> 14:30.380
This concludes the training for hansu pum-se.

14:30.380 --> 14:32.380
We will take another look at all the moves

14:32.380 --> 14:34.900
and master pum-se.

15:02.380 --> 15:04.900
Thank you for watching.

15:32.900 --> 15:35.900
We have looked at the key moves of hansu pum-se

15:35.900 --> 15:37.900
and provided thorough explanations

15:37.900 --> 15:40.900
for each move and things to watch out for.

15:40.900 --> 15:42.900
You will be able to cultivate the spirit

15:42.900 --> 15:46.900
to embrace all and harmony embodied in hansu

15:46.900 --> 15:49.900
if you continue and repeat this training.

15:49.900 --> 15:53.900
We will see you again in the il-yeop pum-se video.

15:53.900 --> 15:55.900
Thanks for watching.

16:02.380 --> 16:04.960
you

